Patch-Id: ASTRA-0006
Title: Exempt the first-party chrome://astra/ UI package from default innerHTML sanitization
Tier: P3
Upstream-Files: dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp
Intent: the product UI is a bundled Svelte app served from chrome://astra/ (jar.mn) and embedded as a chrome-privileged document. Svelte builds every component template with template.innerHTML; the default system-principal sanitization strips button/input/form/script, which made a chrome-privileged mount impossible and forced an out-of-process file:// browser plus a framescript relay. Exempting only documents whose URI begins chrome://astra/ (first-party, fully bundled, no remote or user-controlled markup) lets the UI run as real chrome. Explicit callers (setHTML/setHTMLUnsafe/ParserUtils) keep their own flags and are unaffected.
Risk: medium (touches the fragment-parsing security gate). Scope is one package prefix; any other chrome document keeps the default sanitization. Rollback is deleting the two condition clauses.
Test: tests/contract/shell_app_chrome.py (chrome iframe mounts the app, #root has children, data-bridge-mode=host, first frame complete) + existing live suites
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: drop if Svelte gains a sanitizer-safe template path (or the UI is reimplemented without innerHTML templates)
---
diff --git a/dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp b/dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp
index f127ff4d75..f27f7415a5 100644
--- a/dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp
+++ b/dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp
@@ -6582,6 +6582,36 @@ void nsContentUtils::SetHTMLUnsafe(
 // Please note that about:blank and about:srcdoc inherit the security
 // context from the embedding context and hence are not loaded using
 // an about: scheme principal.
+//
+// ASTRA: the browser's own UI is a bundled Svelte application served from the
+// `chrome://astra/` package (jar.mn). Svelte builds every component template
+// through `template.innerHTML`, and the default system-principal
+// sanitization below strips exactly the elements a component tree needs
+// (button/input/form/script), which made a chrome-privileged mount
+// impossible and forced an out-of-process `file://` browser plus a message
+// relay. That package is first-party, fully bundled code with no remote or
+// user-controlled markup, so it is exempt from the *default* sanitization;
+// explicit callers (`setHTML`/`setHTMLUnsafe`/ParserUtils) keep their flags
+// and are unaffected.
+static bool IsAstraTrustedChromeDocument(dom::Document* aDocument) {
+  if (!aDocument) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  nsIURI* uri = aDocument->GetDocumentURI();
+  if (!uri) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  bool isChrome = false;
+  if (NS_FAILED(uri->SchemeIs("chrome", &isChrome)) || !isChrome) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  nsAutoCString spec;
+  if (NS_FAILED(uri->GetSpec(spec))) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  return StringBeginsWith(spec, "chrome://astra/"_ns);
+}
+
